1
00:04:54,782 --> 00:05:00,782
It can take a lifetime to find true love; she's got 30 days!

2
00:09:49,565 --> 00:09:55,565
The Princess Diaries 2: Royal Engagement is a comedy,
drama, family film directed by Garry Marshall.

3
00:14:44,347 --> 00:14:50,347
Mia Thermopolis is now a college graduate and on her way to
Genovia to take up her duties as princess.

4
00:19:39,130 --> 00:19:45,130
Accompanied by her friend Lilly, Mia continues her 'princess
lessons', like riding horses side-saddle and archery.

5
00:24:33,913 --> 00:24:39,913
But her already complicated life is turned upside down once again when she learns that she is to take the
crown as queen earlier than expected, all while she meets a mysteriously charming young man.

6
00:29:28,695 --> 00:29:34,695
Mia Thermopolis, played by Anne Hathaway.

7
00:34:23,478 --> 00:34:29,478
Queen Clarisse Renaldi, played by Julie Andrews.

8
00:39:18,260 --> 00:39:24,260
Joe, played by Héctor Elizondo.

9
00:44:13,043 --> 00:44:19,043
Viscount Mabrey, played by John Rhys-Davies.

10
00:49:07,826 --> 00:49:13,826
Lilly Moscovitz, played by Heather Matarazzo.

11
00:54:02,608 --> 00:54:08,608
Nicholas Devereaux, played by Chris Pine.

12
00:58:57,391 --> 00:59:03,391
The Princess Diaries 2: Royal Engagement is a 2004 American
romantic comedy film directed by Garry Marshall.

13
01:03:52,173 --> 01:03:58,173
Produced by Walt Disney Pictures, it is the sequel
to 2001's The Princess Diaries.

14
01:08:46,956 --> 01:08:52,956
Unlike the first film, it is not based on any existing book, and has no relation to the second
installment in the book series, The Princess Diaries, Volume II: Princess in the Spotlight.

15
01:13:41,739 --> 01:13:47,739
In the film, Mia Thermopolis learns that before she can succeed her grandmother as
queen of Genovia, she must marry or else relinquish the throne.

16
01:18:36,521 --> 01:18:42,521
Most of the cast returned from the first film, including Anne Hathaway, Julie
Andrews, Héctor Elizondo, Heather Matarazzo, and Larry Miller.

17
01:23:31,304 --> 01:23:37,304
Garry Marshall returned to direct and Debra Martin
Chase and Whitney Houston to produce.

18
01:28:26,086 --> 01:28:32,086
New characters include Viscount Mabrey (John Rhys-Davies), Lord Nicholas Devereaux
(Chris Pine, in his feature film debut), and Andrew Jacoby (Callum Blue).

19
01:33:20,869 --> 01:33:26,869
The film grossed $135.3 million worldwide but received
mixed to unfavorable reviews from critics.

20
01:38:15,652 --> 01:38:21,652
As of 2024, a sequel is in development, with Adele Lim attached as director.

21
01:43:10,434 --> 01:43:16,434
The film explores themes of coronation, marriage, duty, falling in love, calm.

22
01:48:05,217 --> 01:48:11,217
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
